"Website Maintenance Policy (https://grimescountytexas.gov/vertical/sites/%7B958238D0-27E6-4F6C-919E-F1D98542C5FD%7D/uploads/06212023_REGULAR_AGENDA_-_final_-_cc.pdf)\nciteturn5search12 [wordlim: 200] Published: 3.3 years ago; Crawled: 3.3 years ago; The purpose of this website maintenance policy is to ensure the proper maintenance of the County website and make users aware of what Grimes County deems as content, navigation, organization and UX standards on the website. ... Grimes County IT will verify compliance to this policy through various methods, including business tool reports, internal and external audits, and feedback to the policy owner.\nWebsite Maintenance Policy\n\nOverview  \nWebsites are an essential part of any organization today. It is important that the website meet and maintain required operational guidelines as well as maintain a consistent user experience (UX). The document will help provide guidelines for the maintaining of those standards.\n\nPurpose  \nThe purpose of this website maintenance policy is to ensure the proper maintenance of the County website and make users aware of what Grimes County deems as content, navigation, organization and UX standards on the website. This policy outlines the minimum requirements for maintaining the Grimes County Website. This policy to the best of our knowledge adheres to the County and state requirements.\n\nScope  \nThis policy covers appropriate maintenance of the Grimes County website and applies to all employees, vendors, and agents operating on behalf of Grimes County.\n\nPolicy  \n- The IT Director has the right to approve or deny any modifications, additions, and deletions to the website with Commissioners Court having the final authority.\n- The IT Director assigns those employees who will have access and authority to make modifications to, and additions and deletions of content on the website.\n- The IT Director will limit the number of employees that will have access to make modifications, additions, or deletions from the website.\n- IT is responsible for the adherence to state policies and or other regulatory compliance guidelines.\n- IT is responsible for all content hosted on the website.\n- IT is responsible for maintaining DNS records for public access to the site.\n- IT is responsible for maintaining the domain records with dotgov.gov.\n- IT is responsible for always maintaining and making sure the website is operational.\n- IT is responsible for the security of the website.\n- IT is responsible for any SSL certificates that may need to be issued to the site for connectivity, use or compliance.\n- IT is responsible for making sure the website works properly on three most common browsers: Microsoft Edge, Safari, and Google Chrome.\n- It is not responsible for ensuring all users can always access the website from their location and device due to circumstances out of our control.\n\nPolicy Compliance  \nGrimes County IT will verify compliance to this policy through various methods, including business tool reports, internal and external audits, and feedback to the policy owner.\n\nExceptions  \nAny exception to the policy must be approved by the County Judge and Commissioners with the advisement of the IT Director in advance.\n\nNon-Compliance  \nAn employee found to have violated this policy may be subject to disciplinary action, up to and including termination of employment.\n\nRelated Standards, Policies and Processes  \n- None.\n\nDefinitions and Terms  \n- None.\n\nWebsite Maintenance Policy 1.0  \nJune 21, 2023  \nRegular Meeting Agenda\n\nPage 5  \n108--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nGrimes County Commissioners Court (https://granicus_production_attachments.s3.amazonaws.com/grimescountytx/6bc8eb025f42f106300e840db5edaa980.pdf)\nciteturn5search13 [wordlim: 200] Published: 1.1 years ago; Approve Monthly Report submitted by the County Treasurer for July 2025 and authorize ... Presentation of Mo